#Title:    Price Manipulation in Business Logic Flow

#Context:  A lab simulating a business logic flaw in the pricing logic. 

#Feature: Order/Payment work flow

#Expected Invariant: price should be derived and revalidated from a server authoritative source.

On taking the Add to Cart request to my proxy, i modified the price and sent the request and it processed without rejection, then i started another request and modified the price and the item was added to cart with wthe mofified price.
On clicking the checkout button the order was finalized using the modified state.

#Steps To Reproduce:
1) make a request to add an item to cart and intercept it via proxy.
2) Reduce the price and forward the request.
3) Go to cart and finalize order using modified state.

#Broken Invariant:  price was not revalidated from a server authoritative source and a client controlled value was used without recomputation.

#Impact: 
1) direct financial manipulation.
2) pricing arbitrage risk.
3) integrity violation of order state.

#Fix: Pricing must be recompute or revalidated against server-side authoritative data at the final state transition.


